# IoT Modular System — mosquitto ACL template.
# Rendered to /mosquitto/secrets/acl by docker-entrypoint.sh; @@APP_USER@@ and
# @@DEVICE_USER@@ are substituted from MQTT_USER / MQTT_DEVICE_USER.
#
# Model matches the app and the firmware:
#   app    (MQTT_USER)          reads `iot/+/sensors/#`, `iot/+/status`,
#                               writes commands `iot/+/commands`
#   device (MQTT_DEVICE_USER)   firmware logs all devices in with one shared
#                               user ("main" in config.h); each publishes its
#                               own `iot/<id>/sensors/#`, `iot/<id>/status`
#                               and subscribes `iot/<id>/commands/#`
# Anything without a matching rule is denied by default.

user @@APP_USER@@
topic read iot/+/sensors/#
topic read iot/+/status
topic write iot/+/commands

# Shared device user: any device may publish its telemetry (topic carries the
# device id) and read commands addressed to it. For stricter setups give each
# device its own user and add per-user `iot/<id>` rows instead.
user @@DEVICE_USER@@
topic write iot/+/sensors/#
topic write iot/+/status
topic read iot/+/commands/#